        {
          "id": "instructions",
          "type": "note",
          "lines": [
            {
              "b": "Instructions:",
              "t": ""
            },
            "1. Record which product is being made.",
            "2. Using a sanitized Thermapen, measure and record the temperature of the mixture after it has been mixed.",
            "3. Record the time that the mixing has completed.",
            "4. Record the time that the batch is moved into production for use.",
            "5. Record the temperature of the batch when it is moved into production for use.",
            "6. The time between every third batch feeding should be shorter than 4 hours.",
            {
              "b": "Note:",
              "t": "All seafood mix temperatures must be stored in cooler and the internal temperature must remain ≤ 50°F. If temperature is between 50-70°F, it must be used within 5 hours."
            },
            "Sanitize the Thermapen before each use.",
            "Record when last batch of the day enters Production."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
